
# Project Documentation

This directory contains the technical documentation for building, wiring, and testing the Memory Sequence Game.

## Documentation Index

| Document | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `BUILD_GUIDE.md` | Circuit assembly, firmware upload, functional testing, and enclosure fitting. |
| `HARDWARE.md` | Bill of materials and electrical considerations. |
| `PINOUT.md` | Arduino pin assignments and button logic. |

## Recommended Reading Order

1. Start with HARDWARE.md to identify the required components.
2. Review PINOUT.md before connecting the circuit.
3. Follow BUILD_GUIDE.md to assemble, upload, test, and fit the enclosure.

## Documentation Scope

These documents describe the pin assignments and behavior implemented in `firmware/memorygame.ino`.

They are intended as build documentation, not a substitute for component datasheets or board-specific electrical limits.

The repository does not currently include a verified schematic, measured enclosure dimensions, or printer-specific settings.

For the project overview, see the main README.
